A||||2||Spyder||Where exactly on the transaxle does it say which one it is???||||1||
Z||000000||Spyder||03-30-2000||08:32 PM||||Where exactly on the transaxle does it say which one it is???<BR>My transaxle is at my father in laws (hour and a half away) and GT Bastard  wants to buy it if it’s the M19 4 speed.<BR>My paw in law looked on it and only saw a scan tag.  The car it came out of, well, I took off the sticker from on top of the wheel well. It was an 84 SE, any one have a clue. ||||reg||1
Z||000001||cobra427||03-30-2000||09:45 PM||||Spyder,from what I see in the 86 S/M , for the M17&M19 "J" series,the vin location is, as you are at the back of the trunk with the<BR>trans to your left, look down and you will see the two top bellhousing bolts(/**\). Go a little further down the bellhousing on the front side(left side if you were facing the trans from the drivers side rear wheel) and you should come to a flat spot on the edge of the bellhousing where it meets the engine block.That is where the VIN should be for thos two transmissions.It is about 3" down from the two bolts that I've mentioned.<BR>BTW,the "J" series only refers to the M19<BR>Also,FYI the MY8,M19,(1984-4spd),MY8,M17 (1985-86 4spd),are all Muncie.---- The MT2,(85-88-5spd)is an Isuzu.----The MG2,(1986-88 5spd)is also a Muncie.<BR>I hope that this helps.<P>cobra427||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||03-31-2000||12:55 AM||||If it came out of an '84 SE then it will have the M19 tranny (4.10 ratio).  The only other 4-sp. offered in '84 was the MY8, which was a wide ratio (3.32) that was used in the econo-coupe.  Very few of these were produced as most of the 4-spds. in '84 were the M19.||||reg||1
